@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Theming}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_CSS_Variables}")]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Theming_Name @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Core_Variables</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.Theming_Name @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Core_Variables</h1>

<p>The following css custom properties (variables) are used for all components.</p>
<p>
    A component may define its own variables which can accept the base variable values
    or override them, as and when necessary; this allows you very fine grained control.
</p>
<p>
    Changing one base variable will ripple through the system and change everything, but you can, at various stages override this
    behaviour in order to apply a specific value to a specific component without effecting the others.
</p>
<p>
    <strong>Note: </strong>More base variables may be added and/or some default values may be changed but only if they are not currently in use by a released component.
</p>

